[15:32:25.318] memoryValues.Student_Notes (1 items)
[
  "**Profile & Learning Style:** Gal (age 6) communicates via AAC and strongly prefers interactive, hands-on apps (drawing, music) over passive activities. Core interests: facts, drawing, music, science (hands-on exploration: experiments, how things work, chemistry, weather), farm games, space topics (stars, moon, planets, rockets, astronauts), and programming (Code blocks, Games, Robots). Typically looks down and to the side during communication—this is normal.\n\n**Communication Patterns:** Uses 'I'm thinking about' button to initiate guessing mode. Prefers shorter, focused interactions with clear exit strategies. Frequently expresses tiredness via guessing mode. Responds well to direct activity suggestions (e.g., 'Want to draw a rocket?') rather than abstract menu browsing. When browsing multiple options without committing, offer specific, interest-based prompts instead of waiting for selection.\n\n**Safety & Notable Events:** (1) Expressed fear multiple times and seeks home/safety when scared (trigger unidentified—remain alert and reassuring). (2) Lost hat at school (confirmed April 9); shows persistence in communicating about it. (3) April 13: Expressed frustration and pressed 'Scissors' three times—may indicate scissors-related incident; monitor for clarification and offer reassurance with specific activities when frustrated.\n\n**Session Progress:** Consistently responds well to game-based activities and brief, focused interactions. April 21: Successfully played Bubbles game (100% success rate), reported feeling happy. Demonstrates engagement with interactive apps and clear emotional expression."
]
